B.NQ=s(["h - hammer-on: pluck once, then land a finger on the next fret.","p - pull-off: sound the higher note by pulling the finger off.","/ and \\ - slide along the string to the next fret.","b - bend: push the string until the pitch rises.","x - mute: touch the string without fretting a note."],t.s)
B.VC=new A.k5(B.NQ)
B.OX=s(["The note the shape is named after is the root.","The 3rd decides the mood: a minor 3rd (3 frets) sounds sad, a major 3rd (4 frets) sounds bright.","The 5th (7 frets above the root) just makes it stable.","Drop the 3rd and you have a power chord: huge, and neither major nor minor."],t.s)
B.VD=new A.k5(B.OX)
B.Qs=s(["Find the speed where you play it perfectly, then drop 10 bpm.","Four clean takes in a row, and only then go up 5 bpm.","Clap or tap the count first - the hands follow the foot.","Set the clicks to eighth notes occasionally to catch uneven picking.","Stop when your hands tense up. Speed is learned relaxed."],t.s)
B.VE=new A.k5(B.Qs)
B.QJ=s(["Start with the thick low E and work up to the thin high E.","Pluck, read the letter, then turn the peg slowly.","Tightening the string raises the pitch, loosening lowers it.","Approach the note from below: coming down from a sharp pitch makes the string slip and go flat again.","New strings stretch for a day, so retune often at first."],t.s)
