B.du=new A.ib("Theory",8,"theory")
B.VJ=new A.bO("A# and Bb on a guitar are...",B.Qw,0,"Enharmonic notes: same fret, same frequency, different letter depending on the key. This app writes the sharp names.",B.du,null)
B.OP=s(["the same note, at twice the frequency","the note a 5th above","the next string over","the same note, at half the frequency"],t.s)
B.VK=new A.bO("Twelve frets up from any note is...",B.OP,0,"An octave. The 12th fret harmonic rings the same note as the open string because its frequency is exactly double.",B.du,null)
B.P9=s(["singing the same lines gets easier","the strings stay in tune better","it makes the guitar louder","chords become simpler to finger"],t.s)
B.fX=new A.ib("Tunings",6,"tunings")
B.VL=new A.bO("Why do players tune down a half step to Eb?",B.P9,0,"Everything sits a semitone lower, so a key that is awkward to sing drops into reach. The tension on the neck drops with it.",B.fX,null)
B.Px=s(["7","10","12","16"],t.s)
B.VM=new A.bO("How many half steps make up one octave?",B.Px,2,"12 half steps, and the frequency doubles. That is why the 12th fret usually carries two markers.",B.du,null)
B.OQ=s(["the 3rd","the root","the 5th","the tuning"],t.s)
B.VN=new A.bO("E major and E minor use almost the same shape. What makes them different?",B.OQ,0,"Both are built on E and both have a B. One finger moves the 3rd from G# to G, and the mood changes completely.",B.du,null)
B.MR=s(["one extra chromatic note","one note fewer","a raised root","it starts on the 5th"],t.s)
B.em=new A.ib("Scales",4,"scales")
B.VO=new A.bO("What makes the blues scale different from the minor pentatonic?",B.MR,0,"It is the five pentatonic notes plus the flat 5th, six in total. That single passing note is the whole blues sound.",B.em,null)
B.QM=s(["minor pentatonic","harmonic minor","Mixolydian","Dorian"],t.s)
B.VP=new A.bO("Which scale is usually the first one a guitarist learns?",B.QM,0,"Five notes, two per string, and no wrong ones. The minor pentatonic fits over most rock and blues backing tracks straight away.",B.em,null)
B.QH=s(["a full chord just by strumming all six strings","more frets on the neck","lighter string tension only","the ability to skip tuning"],t.s)
B.VQ=new A.bO("What do open tunings like Open G or Open D give you for free?",B.QH,0,"The six open notes are the notes of one chord, which is why a slide or one flat finger across a fret turns the whole neck into a chord.",B.fX,null)
B.P8=s(["only the lowest string","every string drops a whole step","the top two strings","the string order swaps"],t.s)
B.VR=new A.bO("What changes when a guitar goes from E standard to Drop D?",B.P8,0,"One string, two frets down: D2. The rest of the tuning is untouched, which is why every shape you know still works on five strings.",B.fX,null)
B.Pz=s(["they are built from the same seven notes","they share the same root","minor chords always have one note fewer","the tuning stays the same"],t.s)
